      "artist": "DanTD",
      "description": "Two former railroad sidings in the platform between the current and former former Florence Railroad Stations as seen from the entrance to the current station in Florence, South Carolina. The old station was originally a grand Atlantic Coast Line Railroad station, that became an Amtrak Station until 1996, when it moved into a smaller station next door. Now it's just another facility for the McLeod Regional Medical Center, although Amtrak still uses the old platforms. Note the skeletal steel canopy stretching from the station house to some other tracks in the right-of-way.",
